$y=(x+6)^2$, $y=(x-6)^2$, $y=-(x+6)^2$, $y=-(x-6)^2$;

$y=(x+6)^2-9$, $y=(x-6)^2-9$, $y=-(x+6)^2+9$, $y=-(x-6)^2+9$.

Complete the square, then replace $x$ by $-x$ for reflection in the $y$-axis and negate the expression for reflection in the $x$-axis.
